# Tales of Graces f Remastered (PPSA19991) — past the title screen to the new-game Options screen.
#
# VALIDATED on Linux with hardware Vulkan (RADV), native 1920x1080, headless `screenshot`
# frontend, PROSPER_RENDER=1, no render acceleration, 300 s / 30 samples. Observed phases:
#   t~10 s  title screen (474,726 distinct colours)
#   t~30 s  End-User License Agreement, "X Agree / O Disagree / [] Change Language"
#   t~60 s  main menu
#   t~80 s onward  the new-game Options screen (Battle Difficulty / Battle Camera / Message Speed /
#                  Text Auto-Advance / Vibration / Encounters), stable to the end of the run at
#                  35,020-39,396 distinct colours per sample
#
# Cross ONLY. This is the difference from reach-title.pad: the EULA maps Circle to "Disagree", so
# any route that alternates Cross and Circle bounces off the EULA and oscillates back to the title
# screen. Cross alone agrees and proceeds.
#
# Presses are sparse and spread out on purpose — each screen needs one confirmation and then time
# to load, and mashing re-enters submenus.
4-5:cross
6-7:cross
8-9:cross
10-11:cross
12-13:cross
20-21:cross
